// Rule: [T1102.002][T1071.001] Hollowgraph - Hollowgraph Calendar C2
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1102.002, T1071.001
// Classification: Production candidate
// Status: Production candidate
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR
// Required telemetry: MicrosoftGraphActivityLogs
// Purpose: access associated with a covert bidirectional channel.
// Logic: Evaluate MicrosoftGraphActivityLogs for hollowgraph calendar c2 using the existing source-derived conditions while preserving projected investigation context.
// A match proves: A match indicates successful Graph access to the exact far-future calendar range used by the analyzed sample.
// A match does not prove: It does not expose event-body content, attachment names, encrypted data, implant presence or exfiltration success.
// Expected false positives: authorized administration, approved software, testing, or benign artifact collisions.
// Coverage limits: local schema, field population, retention, collection scope, and attacker variation require validation.
// Evidence claims: C001, C002, C003
//
// Title: HOLLOWGRAPH calendar C2 access via Microsoft Graph
// Status: Production candidate
// Confidence: High
// Purpose: Detect successful Microsoft Graph calendarView requests to the
//          exact far-future date observed in the HOLLOWGRAPH sample.
// Required table: MicrosoftGraphActivityLogs
// Required fields: TimeGenerated, RequestMethod, RequestUri,
//                  ResponseStatusCode, AppId, ServicePrincipalId, UserId,
//                  ClientAuthMethod, IPAddress, UserAgent
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1102.002, T1071.001
//
// Important:
// - This is a production candidate, not a production-validated rule.
// - RequestUri must retain the startDateTime query parameter.
// - The rule deliberately does not inspect event subjects, attachment names,
//   or request-body content because MicrosoftGraphActivityLogs does not
//   document those values as available fields.
// - Validate legitimate long-range calendar applications before deployment.

MicrosoftGraphActivityLogs
| where TimeGenerated >= ago(1h)
| where RequestMethod == "GET"
| where RequestUri contains "/calendarView"
| where RequestUri contains "2050-05-13"
| where ResponseStatusCode between (200 .. 299)
| project
    TimeGenerated,
    AppId,
    ServicePrincipalId,
    UserId,
    ClientAuthMethod,
    IPAddress,
    UserAgent,
    RequestMethod,
    RequestUri,
    ResponseStatusCode
